---
import BaseLayout from '../../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
---
<BaseLayout title="AWS Weather Application | Eric Bello" description="Python, Django, API, and AWS weather application by Eric Bello.">
  <section class="project-hero shell narrow">
    <div class="project-meta"><span>Cloud application</span><span>Python · Django · AWS</span></div>
    <h1>AWS Weather Application</h1>
    <p>A cloud hosted application that retrieves live weather data, processes structured API responses, and presents forecast trends through interactive visualizations.</p>
    <div class="hero-actions">
      <a class="button button-primary" href="https://d3lgvgrrop0yu.cloudfront.net/" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">Live demo</a>
      <a class="button button-secondary" href="https://github.com/ericnbello/weather-dashboard" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">View source</a>
    </div>
  </section>
  <section class="case-study shell narrow">
    <div class="case-section"><h2>Overview</h2><p>The application consumes live data from the OpenWeather API, processes the response in a Python and Django stack, and turns forecast data into interactive visualizations.</p></div>
    <div class="case-section"><h2>Environment</h2><ul class="detail-list"><li>OpenWeather REST API as the live data source</li><li>Python for data retrieval and processing</li><li>Django for application logic and API integration</li><li>Plotly for interactive visualization</li><li>AWS services for cloud deployment and delivery</li></ul></div>
    <div class="case-section"><h2>What I implemented</h2><p>I handled external API requests, structured JSON responses, application logic, visualization, and deployment as one end to end technical project.</p></div>
    <div class="case-section emphasis"><h2>What this demonstrates</h2><p>Python development, REST API integration, structured data handling, application deployment, data visualization, and cloud based delivery.</p></div>
  </section>
</BaseLayout>
